## 9. Mandatory debate and handoff order

Use strict round-robin. Do not run agents concurrently against the same mutable worktree or log.

ROUND 0 — ALL:
Read this file, repository AGENTS.md, and current branch state. Confirm exact repository spelling, branch, full HEAD SHA, and worktree status. Record mismatches.

ROUND 1 — CHAT1, lead architect:
Independently map UI → Next.js route → worker route → image_render.py → catalog/resolver → provider adapter → provider API → response/storage/validator. Build candidate matrix. Identify high-confidence root causes and unknowns. Do not edit code.

ROUND 2 — CHAT2, independent adversarial reviewer:
First produce an independent assessment from source and official docs; do not simply adopt CHAT1. Then compare with CHAT1. Challenge scope, assumptions, API version mismatches, unsupported capabilities, frame logic, role order, timeout/fallback safety, and missing tests. Mark every disagreement with evidence. Do not edit code.

ROUND 3 — ARENA AI, test/evidence engineer:
Inspect the same SHA and run only local/no-cost tests. Add mock contract tests only if the user has approved test-file changes; otherwise propose exact tests and run existing tests. Capture final outgoing payload at the HTTP boundary. Distinguish application defects from provider/API failures. No live paid calls. Append exact command/result evidence with secrets removed.

ROUND 4 — CHAT1:
Reconcile findings. Accept/reject each objection with reasons. Publish one ranked root-cause list, minimum-risk architecture, phased patch plan, exact likely files, acceptance criteria, and non-goals.

ROUND 5 — CHAT2:
Perform final adversarial review of the plan. Look for regressions, scope creep, missing cases, false API claims, and unsafe retries. Require a test for every critical invariant.

ROUND 6 — ARENA AI:
Verify that acceptance criteria are testable. Produce the smallest no-cost test matrix. Identify criteria that cannot be verified locally.

ROUND 7 — CHAT1:
Publish the final recommendation to the user. Separate facts, inferences, open decisions, and required approvals. Do not implement until the user approves.

IMPLEMENTATION, ONLY AFTER USER APPROVAL:
- CHAT1 owns one small phase at a time and records exact files/diff.
- CHAT2 reviews the diff independently and requests changes with evidence.
- ARENA AI tests the exact resulting SHA/diff, reports exact results, and checks relevant regressions.
- CHAT1 fixes only validated issues; CHAT2 re-reviews; ARENA AI reruns affected tests.
- Repeat until acceptance criteria pass or a concrete blocker is recorded for the user.

